-=Project Details
Contributors: HARRISON,
Version: 1.3
OS NAME: Axiom
-=Requirements
other than python get in built-in terminal
*python--
get from website:
https://www.python.org/downloads/

*pip
to get on linux(debian-based distro's) type these commands:
sudo apt update
sudo apt install python3-pip
to get on windows/macOS type this command:
py -m ensurepip --upgrade

verify installation:
python -m pip --version

*OpenCV--
to get on linux/macOS type this command:
python3 -m pip install opencv-python
to get on windows type this command:
py -m pip install opencv-python

verify installation(recommended):
1. make python file
2. put in:
import cv2
print(cv2.__version__)

Contrib Modules(optional):
pip install opencv-contrib-python

NOTE: this file system repsitory uses linux file systems if you have another OS check your file applicaition to fix the path then fix it in the code. you can always reinstall the file.
